   Four-way condition: native kt: guard | In() predicate | safeEvaluateGuard()
   | static Kotlin.

   The native arm comes first, as it does for a transition. Without it a
   `kt:` cond fell to the constant fold at the end and became
   `if (false)`, which made the branch body dead code and ran any `else`
   beside it unconditionally — a wrong output with no diagnostic. #}
